    {
      "name": "TTS reliability",
      "description": "Fixes text-to-speech reading that stops after a phone call or does nothing when pressing play: re-creates the TTS engine when it dies, pauses during calls and resumes afterwards, retries failed lines, uses the correct Vietnamese voice, and applies a new speed right away instead of after pause + play. A stopped line goes on from the word it was stopped at (pause, lock screen, call, speed change, reopening the book), not from its start. \"~\" and \"...\" are read naturally (\"1~2\" = \"1 đến 2\", a short pause after \"...\", quotes around \"...\" are not read).",
      "default": true,
